  "goodToKnow": "Der Torf is peat, formed in Moore (bogs) over thousands of years. It was once cut (gestochen) and burned as fuel in northern Germany, and it's used in potting soil. Since intact bogs store huge amounts of carbon, Germany plans to phase out peat in hobby gardening, and torffreie Erde is spreading. Related to English turf. It has no plural."
